course: dictionary
lesson: 11874
title: The bowsprit
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A bowsprit is a long pole that sticks out forward from the front of a sailing ship. The bow is the front of a ship, so the bowsprit is the pole at the front. «The sailors climbed out along the bowsprit to fix the front sail.» Climbing out along a pole that sticks out from the front fits the meaning, so the clues help you.
explain: The bowsprit is a spar, a strong pole that the ropes of the front sails are tied to. «The ropes of the front sails were tied to the bowsprit.» Try the swap check: put «the long pole at the front» in place of bowsprit. The sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: You may meet bowsprits in pirate stories, sea tales and The Wind in the Willows, where the Sea Rat tells of his voyages. In history lessons about sailing ships, the bowsprit is one of the parts you need to know.
fact: A bowsprit is a long pole sticking out forward from the front of a sailing ship.
fact: The bow is the front of a ship.
fact: A spar is a strong pole that the ropes of a sail are tied to.
fact: Sailors climb out on the bowsprit to handle the front sails, which are called jibs.
fact: Bowsprit is pronounced BOH-sprit, and the plural is bowsprits.
exercise: «The sailors climbed out along the bowsprit to fix the front sail.» What is a bowsprit? | A small room below the deck | The back of a ship where the flag flies | *A long pole sticking out from the front of a ship | A rope used to pull up the anchor
exercise: Which part of a ship is the bow? | The middle deck | *The front | The bottom of the sea | The back
exercise: «The ropes of the front sails were tied to the bowsprit.» Where were the ropes tied? | *To the bowsprit | To the captain's hat | To the anchor | To the bottom of the sea
test: «The pirate ship sped across the waves, its bowsprit cutting through the spray.» Where is the bowsprit? | Inside the cabin | *At the front of the ship | Under the water only | At the back of the ship
test: Which word means the front of a ship? | Mast | *Bow | Hull | Stern
exam: «On a sailing ship, the front sails were tied to the bowsprit, so sailors climbed out along it.» What is the bowsprit? | *A long pole at the front of the ship | A sail at the back of the ship | A deck where guests dine | A ring for the anchor
